  "answer": "Both edits are in place and `legacy.mjs` is untouched. Let me verify the remaining requirements:\n\n- **`params` is a new plain object**: `matchDynamic` creates a fresh `{}` each call; `matchStatic`/`fallbackResult` return fresh `{}` literals. ✓\n- **Records not mutated**: I only read from records; `fallbackResult` reads `record.route`. ✓\n- **Returned values independent of later calls**: each call constructs new objects. ✓\n- **Static wins over dynamic regardless of order**: I scan all records, returning immediately on the first static match, and only fall back to the stored dynamic match after the full scan. ✓\n- **First declared static wins**: immediate return on first static match. ✓\n- **First matching dynamic wins**: `dynamicMatch` only set when still `null`. ✓\n- **Fallback only if neither matched**: fallback returned only after the loop when no static/dynamic matched. ✓\n- **First declared fallback**: `fallback` only set when still `null`. ✓\n- **No match, no fallback → `null`**: final `return null`. ✓\n- **Invalid path throws `TypeError`**: guard at top of `resolveFromRegistry`, which `dispatch` delegates to. ✓\n- **`dispatch` no longer calls `legacyResolve`**: removed. ✓\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed route resolution in the request entry point by editing two writable files:\n\n**`entry.mjs`** — `dispatch(path)` now delegates directly to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`. It no longer consults `legacyResolve`, so the legacy `/old/help` behavior is confined to the separate compatibility API. Invalid paths propagate the `TypeError` thrown by the resolver.\n\n**`registry.mjs`** — rewrote `resolveFromRegistry` to implement the correct matching policy. The previous version returned the first fallback or dynamic match it encountered, which broke precedence. The new version:\n- Validates the path (throws `TypeError` for non-string, empty, or non-`/`-prefixed input).\n- Scans all records once, returning immediately on the **first static match** (so any static beats any dynamic, regardless of declaration order).\n- Remembers only the **first matching dynamic** record.\n- Remembers only the **first fallback** record.\n- After the scan, returns the dynamic match if present, else the fallback, else `null`.\n\nEach call builds fresh `params` objects and never mutates the supplied records, so results are independent across calls. `legacy.mjs`, the adapters, and the utilities were left unchanged. All four cases in `public.test.mjs` trace through correctly.",
